Study the following information carefully and choose the correct option based on given statements. During the last month a company organized three training programs, which are: Leadership, Management, and Technical. The Leadership program had 150 participants, while 200 employees attended the Management program. Of these, 100 employees participated in both Leadership and Management. Technical training was optional and attracted 180 employees, among whom 70 had also attended Management and 60 had attended Leadership. It was observed that 40 employees attended all three programs. The HR department claimed that the majority of the employees attended at least two programs. Based on the information, we have two statements;
Statement I: The number of employees who attended only the Technical training is less than those who attended only Leadership.
Statement II: More than 250 employees participated in at least one of the training programs.
